# Three tool rounds

## Section

This Agent uses one Action in three dependent ReAct rounds. The mock script
fixes the sequence; a real model can choose a different sequence. Change only
`backend` to `:live` to explore it with `OPENAI_API_KEY`.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

script = [
  %{reply: {:tools, [%{id: "first", name: "multiply", arguments: %{a: 2, b: 3}}]}},
  %{reply: {:tools, [%{id: "second", name: "multiply", arguments: %{a: 6, b: 4}}]}},
  %{reply: {:tools, [%{id: "third", name: "multiply", arguments: %{a: 24, b: 5}}]}},
  %{reply: {:text, "The final product is 120."}}
]

mock = if backend == :mock, do: elem(Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(script: script), 1)
context = if mock, do: %{ai: %{assistant: %{options: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)}}}, else: %{}
```

## Define the Action and Agent

```elixir
defmodule Guide.Multiply do
  use Jido.Action,
    name: "guide_multiply",
    schema: Zoi.object(%{a: Zoi.integer(), b: Zoi.integer()})

  @impl Jido.Action
  def run(%{a: a, b: b}, _context), do: {:ok, %{value: a * b}}
end

defmodule Guide.ThreeRounds do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_three_rounds"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{answer: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default("")})

    ai :assistant do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      instructions "Use multiply once per round. Use each result in the next call."
      reasoning :react

      tools do
        action Guide.Multiply, as: :multiply
      end

      controls do
        timeout 30_000
        max_iterations 4
        max_model_calls 4
        max_tool_calls 3
      end

      result into: :answer
    end
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/ai/three_tool_rounds"

    route "guides.ai.three_rounds", ai: :assistant do
      define :calculate, args: [:query]
    end
  end
end
```

## Run and inspect

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(Guide.ThreeRounds, id: "guide-three-rounds")

{:ok, answer} =
  Guide.ThreeRounds.ask_sync(
    server,
    "Multiply 2 by 3, that result by 4, and that result by 5. Use the tool for each step.",
    context: context
  )

%{answer: answer, stored_answer: Jido.AgentServer.agent(server).state.answer}
```

In mock mode, the fourth provider request follows three tool results. Inspect
the request count and names. Live mode can use fewer or different calls.

```elixir
if mock do
  report = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: [], requests: [_, _, _, _]} = report
  Enum.map(report.requests, & &1.body["model"])
end
```

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Add a tool and ReAct](../v3/02_tools_and_react.md).
